    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onboarding_step">Step %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Welcome to Lockdown App</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">Your phone is designed to capture your attention.\n\nThis app helps you reclaim it. Create scheduled periods where distractions are unavailable.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_strong_title">How strong lockdown works</string>
    <string name="onboarding_strong_body">For the strongest enforcement, this device needs to be provisioned as a managed (Device Owner) device.\n\nThis is an official Android security feature, not an exploit. Without it, Lockdown App uses screen pinning, which you can leave at any time.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_learn_more">As Device Owner, Lockdown App can keep the phone in lock task (kiosk) mode during a session: only the apps you allow can open, Home returns to the focus screen, the notification shade and recents are unavailable, and the app cannot be uninstalled or force-stopped until the session ends.\n\nDevice Owner can normally only be set on a freshly reset device (or a test device without accounts) using ADB, a QR code, or an enterprise enrollment service. The Device setup screen has exact instructions.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_safety_title">Your safety comes first</string>
    <string name="onboarding_safety_body">Once a session starts, you cannot voluntarily end it from the app.\n\nLockdown App never blocks emergency calls, the power menu, the secure lock screen, or Android\'s recovery and factory-reset mechanisms. These always remain available by design.</string>

