    <string name="setup_how_title">How strong lockdown works</string>
    <string name="setup_how_body">Android only lets a Device Owner app keep the phone in lock task (kiosk) mode, restrict Settings and prevent uninstalling. Device Owner is an official Android Enterprise feature. It must be set up deliberately; Lockdown App never acquires it on its own.</string>
    <string name="setup_dev_title">Development / testing (ADB)</string>
    <string name="setup_dev_steps">1. Use a test device or emulator. Remove all accounts (Settings › Accounts) or factory reset it and skip account setup.\n2. Enable USB debugging and connect the device.\n3. Run:</string>
    <string name="setup_dev_verify">4. Verify the result:</string>
    <string name="setup_dev_notes">If the command fails with “already has accounts” or “already provisioned”, the device must be reset first. To undo, use Settings › Remove device management in this app, or factory reset the device.</string>
    <string name="setup_production_title">Production</string>
    <string name="setup_production_body">For devices you distribute, provision Lockdown App as Device Owner during setup using QR-code provisioning, NFC, or zero-touch / an EMM. Existing consumer phones with accounts cannot become managed without a factory reset.</string>
    <string name="setup_safety_title">Always available</string>
    <string name="setup_safety_body">Emergency calls, the power menu, the secure lock screen, recovery mode and factory reset are never blocked.</string>

